WEBVTT

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.800
To put it bluntly...

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.000
Even not so bluntly...

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.360
They're dead.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.130
To put it bluntly,
this ship is dead, too.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.060
Lilith, don't you
know how to fix it?

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.330
I just lost my appetite.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.230
Lala?

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.260
Yes?

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.630
To put it bluntly,
all the adults are dead.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.060
Dead?

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.560
Maybe it was a plague or something
but they're definitely not alive.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:52.830
Not alive?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.260
In other words, all their vital signs
and activities have ceased functioning.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.860
Is that what you call "death"?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.700
That's exactly what I'm saying.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.760
Just as I suspected.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.560
I've never lived, so I don't
know what death is like.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.960
I know it too well.
Death is the final parting.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.360
The most painful goodbye.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.160
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.260
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.500
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.600
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:43.530
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:50.330
...was the only truth there was.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:58.160
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:07.700
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.600
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.730
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:24.500
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.430
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:34.430
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:39.400
I'll keep searching for you.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.760
Tamamo no Mae

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.900
I was certain that I
felt Hatsumi's presence.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:04.060
Is this really
just a colony ship?

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.100
Now then...

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:32.800
Rocket! Rocket!

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.330
An earth-like planet?

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.260
Oh my, how many
lives do I need to survive?

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.060
Miss Lilith,
where have you been?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.900
Say, Lala, is there
enough energy for a warp?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.830
Yes, probably just
enough for one more.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.830
I found a nice planet
4 light years from here.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.200
Leila?

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.300
Miss Hazuki.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.460
I didn't know a forest
like this existed here?

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.330
I like it here.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.160
The air is so clean.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.800
Indeed.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.960
This is also
where Miss Lulau was.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:33.660
Miss Lulau?

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:34.660
Yes.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:35.860
Who's that?

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.760
Miss Lulau appeared in this
forest more than 100 years ago.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.760
At that time she was still a
baby and raised as a child of god.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.000
What happened to her?

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.600
While working
outside the spaceship,...

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:56.460
...she was sucked into a
dark hole and never returned.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.500
She's my idol.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.400
Did it happen on her 16th birthday?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.960
How did you know that?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.600
She was here.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.660
I knew you would be here.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:11.960
Lamuro!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.760
Lala wants us to
return to the ship.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.430
It seems like
we're going to warp.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.030
Warp, why all of a sudden?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.360
Looks like things are
getting pretty serious.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:41.530
I guess so.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:42.930
Look at that planet.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.460
It looks just like earth.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.960
Where have you been?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:49.460
Hi!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.860
Attention everybody.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.300
For these past 200 years,...

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.100
...we have been searching
for our own planet to colonize.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.430
Now our search is finally over.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.600
We will check this
planet within the next few days.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:13.100
If everything is fine,
we will prepare to land soon.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.130
Please prepare your
belongings for a smooth transition.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.030
Yes, sir!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.160
We must choose a
name for our new home planet.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:23.830
Yes!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.030
Leila.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.160
I think the planet
should be named "Lulau".

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.730
I wonder what it's like
to stand in the sun light?

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.260
You'll soon find out.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.160
True.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.060
There is a malfunction.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:48.130
The automatic planet detection
device on the exterior of the ship...

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.030
...has malfunctioned.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:58.900
Any volunteers for this repair
mission must report to gate 1.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.060
I'll do it.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.600
It's too much for a girl, I'll go.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.160
You're not good at this stuff.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:11.060
I had a lecture about
this kind of work from Leila.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.430
Is that right?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.300
In that case, we'll have Leila do it.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.360
Yes!

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:21.930
The signal has stopped in the
C-2 area of the evacuation pod.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.160
All parts need to be
replaced in that unit.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:25.730
Yes.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.460
Lulau, please protect me.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:26.960
Thank god you're okay.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:27.660
Lamuro.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:32.060
Let's get married on that planet.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.960
Hey hold on a minute.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.900
Not now, it's filthy.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:16.300
You will all move to Planet
Lulau to begin a new life.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.160
This ship is not equipped
with a landing system.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.830
Each section must
board the small ships to land.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.560
Mother, let's go.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.130
Leila.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:30.330
What is it?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.160
You go on ahead.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:33.860
But...

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.130
Hurry, Lamuro must
be waiting for you, right?

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.130
Yes.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.830
Okay, so see you later.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.700
Please rest now.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:03.630
Leila.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.560
What are you going to do now?

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.860
We'll be going to another world,
so this is goodbye.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.230
Thank you for everything,
mysterious people.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.160
This is something from Lala.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:21.230
What is it?

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:25.160
This is the DNA data of many
different life forms from earth.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.300
You will be able to recreate...

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.360
...many of earth's plants
and animals in the new world.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.530
Thank you!

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.600
We are ready for take off.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:39.000
- Good bye, thank you!
- Please fasten your seat belts.

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:41.300
Good bye.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.160
Good bye, Leila.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.000
What a beautiful planet.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.360
Where are we landing, Lala?

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:57.630
Lala?

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:01.130
Where's Lala?
Is she not on this shuttle?

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:07.900
This will be my
last message to you.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:14.900
Upon delivering you to this new
planet, my mission is now complete.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.360
If you remember
what we studied together,...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:21.730
...you can use that knowledge...

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:25.160
...to create a comfortable,
new world very soon.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:34.700
I will pray that your new
world is full of happiness.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.060
Good bye, my children.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:12.700
Lala.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:13.660
Yes?

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:15.630
Aren't you lonely now?

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:16.830
No.

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:21.100
Neither loneliness
nor death exist for me.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:25.730
A moment and
eternity are the same to me.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:31.300
I will remain here and
look upon the new world.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:56.560
It's rather sudden, but let us
return to the Universal Gardens.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:01.630
It seems to be quite a
tense situation here...

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.130
Princess Mariel!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.200
Yes?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.060
My name is Mau.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:11.800
Mau?

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:17.030
Oh, so your old name was Mariel.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.600
No, I don't know such a woman!

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.100
Listen, she used to be a frog.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:24.730
A frog?

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:28.600
Yes, that was...

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.630
The Male Killer

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.300
Oh my!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.230
What are you trying
to do, stupid frog!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.460
I see, you've got the
spirit of someone inside you.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.900
I feel sorry for you,
trapped in such a form.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.460
Okay, leave it to me!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.000
Well, you're
looking pretty good, missy.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.030
What's your name?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.360
You don't remember?

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:29.800
Sometimes it's better that way.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.930
So that's how she ended up here.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.160
She has no memory?

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:48.100
Oh, mister... it looks
like you're hurting here.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:52.060
You don't say?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.700
She smells nice!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.460
What are you doing to her!

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.560
Can they swim?

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.160
I could care less.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.600
I'll go find them.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:32.530
Your shadows.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:34.960
Drink up.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.360
You make me laugh.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:46.260
My shadows? They're
merely my servants.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.860
Still they are your creation.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:53.260
You can't make
something that isn't part of you.

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:58.000
Which means, those
three are part of you.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.730
You remember Meirin?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.160
She's my shadow.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.630
Don't associate those
three with a part of me!

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:11.930
You're mocking yourself, so uncool.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:19.500
It's cowardly to deny your
weakness as a man, no, as a human!

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:25.460
I'm not cowardly or weak!

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.300
I am the chosen one to rule this world!

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.900
I am the chosen one...

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:53.630
..so why do I feel this way now?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:02.560
Well, loosen up... be my
guest and have a drink.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.760
Ouch! That hurt!

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.800
Such a gigantic butt!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:17.500
Shut up!

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.200
Chance!

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:29.700
No, the mattress is
so soft I can't get up!

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:40.730
Where are we?

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.660
The Universal Gardens.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.530
I guess we came back
to Tamamo no Mae's place.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.560
We may never get out of
here if we get lost again!

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.300
Even so...

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.300
If there's a
chance Hatsumi's here!

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.830
Hazuki, wait for me!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.330
I thought we were dead!

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:09.930
I thought I was done for!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.460
I drank too much water!

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.360
What's wrong, Guriel?

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:32.500
Did you hurt your
hand where you burned it?

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.560
Sea water must have
gotten in the wound?

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.530
It hurts!

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:47.830
Oh my!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:48.830
You poor thing!

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.000
Be calm.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:02.860
When we get back,
let's put some balm on it.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.060
Those women are true witches.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:16.060
To marry one of
them would be pure hell.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:26.630
Are you okay?

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:38.430
Oh my goodness!

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.400
This one's empty, too.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.660
You are quite a big drinker, yourself.

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:55.130
Master!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.360
Guriel's in big trouble!

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.930
He's going to get married!

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:03.360
My bride!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.400
Is somebody there?

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.760
Who are you?

00:20:12.430 --> 00:20:13.400
And who are you!?

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.600
There you are, Hazuki!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:21.660
Scary hat!

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:28.360
Is Lilith's hat really that scary?

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:43.760
Meanie, give me back my hat!

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.530
It's not what I expected.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:51.330
She seems very weak.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:55.030
She seems far prettier than usual.

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:55.960
Don't be fooled!

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:57.300
She is faking it.

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.660
I am not faking it!

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.560
I did nothing wrong.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.230
It's quite noisy here.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:28.960
Hatsumi!

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:29.800
Jill!

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:31.930
Eve.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:53.400
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:59.830
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:07.300
I will go there, praying.

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:14.130
No matter the distance
between us, I will catch you.

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:21.960
That's a promise between you and I.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:29.300
Crying, cradling my memories,...

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:35.800
...won't help even one
of my feelings to reach you.

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:44.830
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:51.460
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:53.430 --> 00:23:00.360
I will find the dawn
between you and I,...

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:08.800
...and meet the approaching daybreak.

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:14.030
I will go there, praying.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:19.630
How dare Eve show up this late!
I'm gonna eat and eat to cool down!

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:20.860
Chomp! Chomp!

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:22.730
Let's take a look at the next book.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:53.530
Next Time: Gargantua
Yami, the Hat, and the Book Traveler.

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:56.100
Please enjoy the next story as well.
